==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|upland}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ūpland|t=the country}}; equivalent to {{pre|en|up|land}}. 

The word as an adjective developed in Middle English.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[area]] in the [[interior]] of a [[country]] with a [[generally]] [[higher]] [[elevation]]; often [[hilly]], but not generally [[mountainous]] (compare [[highland]]s).
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[country]], as against the [[town]].

